  booktitle={2026 International Conference on Integrated Intelligence and Cognitive Engineering (ICIICE)}, 
  title={Hybrid Forecasting of Occlusal Changes in Deep Bite Correction Based on Digital Setup, 3D Models, and Design Factors}, 
  year={2026},
  volume={},
  number={},
  pages={1-6},
  abstract={This study presented a reproducible protocol for hybrid prediction of underachievement in vertical tooth movements during deep bite correction with clear aligners. The methodology integrates digital setup data, morphometric parameters derived from 3D models, and biomechanical design factors, including attachment configuration and interproximal reduction (IPR) protocols. The article described an algorithm for constructing multimodal datasets and a standardized 3D superimposition workflow, followed by feature extraction using both engineered descriptors (e.g., depth of the Curve of Spee) and neural network architectures for point clouds (Point Transformers). The proposed computational pipeline incorporates measurement accuracy validation modules and stress-testing procedures across different clinical subgroups (extraction cases, various aligner change regimens). The study aims to establish a technological foundation for clinical decision support systems that enable proactive adaptation of treatment design and improve the predictability of orthodontic therapy. To demonstrate the feasibility of the proposed protocol in the absence of publicly available clinical datasets, a proof-of-concept analysis is conducted on a synthetic dataset.},
  keywords={Modeling;Planning;Teeth;Printing;Design methodology;Equations;Measurement;Three-dimensional displays;Aluminum;Intellectual property;deep bite;overbite correction;3D superimposition;digital orthodontics;machine learning;clinical decision support;clear aligner therapy;point transformers;treatment expression},
